  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1120 AM CST Mon Nov 23 2026\n\nHeights rebuild quickly Tuesday night downstream of a flattening \nupper ridge that keeps things quiet through Thanksgiving. At the \nsurface, a cool ridge anchored roughly along the I35 corridor from \nKansas to the Texas Rio Grande Valley is shown to move very little \nthrough Thanksgiving, but will undergo warming which supports milder \nhighs for us through the end of the week. NBM's highs are stubbornly \nslow to catch onto this warming theme with most of its highs by \nThanksgiving and Friday still trailing MOS and deterministic output \nby a large margin. The earlier dampening ridge aloft will be \nreplaced by weakly cyclonic NW flow by Thursday night, complete with \na shortwave trough sometime Friday with a weak cold front on its \nheels. Moisture is quite barren in this regime, so precip \nchances remain nil through Sunday.",
